course: dictionary
lesson: 1575
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A capital letter often tells you a word is a name, not an ordinary word. Charlotte is a girl's name, so it tells you who someone is, not what something means. «Charlotte orders des chips in a café in Calais» is a story about a person.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so check the context. A small c changes everything: a charlotte is a pudding. In a recipe, «apple charlotte» is a dessert, not a person.
explain: Ask: is this a name or a thing? Look at the words around it. A name is used in stories and about people or places. A pudding is used in cooking and recipes. Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Charlotte is a girl's name, and also the name of a city in North Carolina, USA.
fact: A charlotte (small c) is a pudding made with fruit or cream inside a case of bread, sponge cake or sponge fingers.
fact: «Apple charlotte» is one example of this dessert.
fact: Context tells you which meaning is right: a name in a story, or a food in a recipe.
exercise: «Charlotte orders des chips in a café in Calais.» Is Charlotte a name or a food? | A sponge cake | *A name, a girl's name | A bag of crisps | A pudding made with fruit
exercise: Which of these is a dessert? | *Apple charlotte | Charlotte, North Carolina | Charlotte the spider | Charlotte's Web
exercise: The word Charlotte with a capital C is usually what? | A sponge cake | A pudding | A fruit | *A name
test: In a recipe, what does a charlotte with a small c mean? | *A pudding with fruit or cream inside a case | A girl's name | A clever spider | A city in the USA
test: «Charlotte is a city in North Carolina, USA.» In this sentence, Charlotte is a | *name of a place | pudding | crisp | spider
exam: In the café in Calais, what does Charlotte get when she orders des chips? | A slice of apple charlotte | Hot chips, as she expected | *A bag of crisps | Des frites, which are crisps
